  "narrative": {
    "intro": "KBR Wyle Services obligated $531M in FY2026 to date across 132 awards, with an average award size of $4M and obligations down 17.0% year over year. KBR Wyle Services has a multiyear presence in federal markets, with obligations rising from $278M in FY21 to a peak of $640M in FY25 before the current-year level of $531M. KBR Wyle Services is concentrated with a few large buyers: the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $339M, the Department of the Interior obligated $71.5M, and the Department of Defense obligated $53.8M. KBR Wyle Services sells a mix of technical and support services. The largest NAICS markets for KBR Wyle Services are Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $147M and Engineering Services at $131M. KBR Wyle Services also records significant activity in Computer Facilities Management Services at $67.9M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) at $63.7M. These concentrations explain the vendor's federal footprint in FY2026 to date.",
